      "Roles multiply everything. One user type is one product. Add a second role — an admin, a provider, a customer — and you have built a second interface, a second set of permissions, and a second list of edge cases. Most budget blowouts trace back to a role that was \"obviously included\" and never scoped.",
      "Integrations are priced like features but behave like dependencies. Payments, maps, messaging, accounting — each one is someone else's system, with its own rules, fees and failure modes. An MVP with three integrations is a different project from an MVP with none, even if the screens look identical.",
