      "Your phone already knows how much money you lose to missed calls — it is sitting in the call log, unreturned. Most callers who reach voicemail do not leave a message and do not call back; they dial the next business on the list while the intent is still warm. This guide does the missed-call maths with your own numbers, then compares the three ways businesses actually solve it: self-serve AI receptionist tools, a human answering service, and a managed AI calling agent — including where each one is the wrong choice.",
      "## First, do your own maths",
      "Take last month's call log and count the calls that rang out, hit voicemail, or arrived outside working hours. Multiply by two honest numbers: the share of those callers who were real buyers (for most service businesses, a third to a half), and the average value of one job, booking or case. A clinic missing 40 calls a month, where a third were patients and an average booking is worth $150, is leaving roughly $2,000 a month on the table. A home-services firm with $400 average jobs leaves more. Your number will differ — the point is that for most businesses it is not small, and it recurs every month, silently.",
      "Now price the fixes against that number, not against zero.",
      "## Option 1: Self-serve AI receptionist tools ($29–$599/mo)",
